Fixtures for the tests in tests/. All are trimmed to what the parsers read.

Real captures from a Steam Machine on SteamOS 3.9.5 (connector HDMI-A-1, FRL 4K144 HDR and TMDS 4K60,
both with a BT2020_RGB Colorspace):
  modetest.frl-hdr, modetest.tmds-4k60   modetest -e -c -p, HDMI-A-1 and CRTC 0 kept
  dtn_log.frl-hdr, dtn_log.tmds-4k60     amdgpu_dm_dtn_log, tables the parsers read kept
  crtc/frl-hdr, crtc/tmds-4k60           crtc-0/amdgpu_current_bpc and
                                         amdgpu_current_colorspace (the colorspace
                                         file has no trailing newline; idle CRTCs
                                         fail with ENODEV, so they are not here)

Derived by editing a real capture, not captured:
  modetest.tmds-4k120          tmds-4k60 with CRTC 0 running 3840x2160@120 (1188000 kHz)
  modetest.tmds-4k60-default   tmds-4k60 with the connector Colorspace property at Default
  dtn_log.frl-420              frl-hdr with the HPO row at 4:2:0, depth 8
  dtn_log.frl-reordered        frl-hdr with Depth and Pixel Format swapped, header and row
  crtc/frl-420, crtc/tmds-4k120   8 bpc, BT2020_YCC
  crtc/tmds-4k60-default          8 bpc, BT709_YCC

The older modetest.* and dtn_log.* files (120hz-*, 144hz, frl, tmds, ...) are
hand-made for tests/frl-detect.sh.

ALLM fixtures, all derived (the patched module that writes them is not in the
captures):
  crtc/frl-hdr-allm, -allm-off, -allm-unknown   frl-hdr plus crtc-0/amdgpu_current_hdmi
                                                as patch 0003 prints it: DC content
                                                type 8 (game) with ALLM on, 1 (graphics)
                                                with it off, and 3 (not a DC value)
  modparam/*/hdmi_allm_default                  /sys/module/amdgpu/parameters
  grubd/*/hdmi21-allm.cfg                       what hdmi-allm.sh writes
